```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason:  
All three scripts return the same four (container,item) pairs, but `1result.sql` is the most robust and therefore the safest correct choice.

• It restricts the recursion to start only from true top‑level containers, so it does no unnecessary work yet still explores every deeper level.  
• It converts the contained item id to a readable name even when that id is a *product* rather than another piece of packaging, by UNION‑ing the packaging and products tables (`item_names` CTE).  
• The logic for identifying top‑level containers and for multiplying / summing quantities follows the specification exactly; the resulting output matches the expected data.